@啦不啦咯

Redness, swelling, and itching are all normal parts of the immune response to getting a tattoo. In fact, the immune response is responsible for preserving tattoos as permanent marks on the body. However, tattoos may also have lasting effects on the immune system—with studies linking them to increased cancer risk. Mounting evidence suggests tattoos are linked to elevated cancer risk.&nbsp;
While tattoos continue to become ever more prevalent, recent years have brought a steady drumbeat of scientific studies linking tattoo ink to an elevated cancer risk—findings that might give you pause if you’re thinking about getting one.
